\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The Glory of the spring how sweet,
\par The new-born life how glad;
\par What joy the happy earth to greet
\par In new, bright raiment clad.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Divine Renewer, Thee I bless;
\par I greet Thy going forth:
\par I love Thee in the loveliness
\par Of Thy renewed earth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But O these wonders of Thy grace,
\par These nobler works of Thine,
\par These marvels sweeter far to trace,
\par These new births more divine!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. This new-born glow of faith so strong,
\par This bloom of love so fair,
\par This new-born ecstasy of song,
\par And fragrancy of prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Creator Spirit, work in me
\par These wonders sweet of Thine;
\par Divine Renewer, graciously
\par Renew this heart of mine.
\par                              Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

